.TH CPIO 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cpio \- copie des fichiers vers et depuis des archives / copy files to and from archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpio
-o [-H newc|odc] [-v] < list > archive
.br
.B cpio
-i [-dmuvt] [pattern...] < archive
.br
.B cpio
-p [-dmv] directory < list
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads and writes newc (070701, and 070702 when reading) and odc (070707) archives: regular files, directories, symbolic links, devices and pipes. Hard links are
stored as separate copies on output and rebuilt from GNU archives on input. -d creates leading directories, -u overwrites, -t lists, -v is verbose.
.SH SEE ALSO
tar(1), find(1)
